---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../design/kit/astro/Hero.astro';
import landscape from '../assets/landscape.jpg';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" description="About the Swiss Minimal design kit.">
  <Hero
    title="About"
    lead="Swiss Minimal is a small design kit for type-led sites: one grotesque typeface, flat color, thick rules and almost no decoration."
    image={landscape}
    alt="Wide crop of an abstract composition: a red circle, black and grey shapes and thin black rules"
    caption="A 16:9 crop of the home page artwork, to show the wide hero."
  />
  <article class="max-w-2xl pb-16 [&>p]:mb-5">
    <p>
      This page exists to check the type scale on running text. Body copy sits at 16px with a line height of
      1.5, which keeps paragraphs open without feeling loose. Headings rely on size and weight alone; there are
      no colored headings, no boxes and no icons to prop them up.
    </p>
    <p>
      The palette is three colors and a red. Cream paper, near-black ink, a muted grey for secondary text, and
      one brand red kept for large shapes and the focus ring. Small red text uses a darker tone on the page so
      it still passes contrast.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each page of the menu has its own link. Write to us on the
      <a class="link" href="#contact">contact page</a>, or see the <a class="link" href="#features">features</a>
      and when each arrived.
    </p>
    <p>
      Code is the one place a second family appears. To start a site, copy <code>kit/</code> and
      <code>fonts/</code> into <code>src/design/</code> and import the kit from your global stylesheet; press
      <kbd>Tab</kbd> to see the focus ring.
    </p>
    <pre class="mb-5" tabindex="0"><code>@import "../design/kit/tailwind.css";
/* site-only CSS below */</code></pre>
    <p class="small muted">
      Set in Overused Grotesk, released under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
